.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-WEBUI 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-webui
.Nd the kldload web console: install, virtual machines, clusters, storage and more, from a browser
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -unix-socket Ar path
.Op Fl -port Ar port
.Op Fl -bind Ar address
.Op Fl -no-tls
.Op Fl -no-browser
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
serves the web console's pages and the WebSocket its pages use to act on
the machine, as root: installing, making and deleting virtual machines,
building clusters, opening terminals.
On an installed machine
.Pa kldload-webui.service
runs it on a unix socket that only
.Xr nginx 8
reaches, and nginx serves it on port 8443 with the machine's certificate.
.Pp
Who may act:
.Bl -tag -width "on the live image"
.It on the live image
anyone at the console, for the install;
.It from this machine
anyone, without a password: the request came through nginx from
loopback, which only nginx can claim on that socket;
.It from elsewhere
a member of the administrators' group
.Pq Ql wheel No or Ql sudo
with their system password, checked by PAM, or the bearer token in
.Pa /etc/kldload/webui-token
for scripts.
.El
.Pp
If PAM cannot be used the password is refused.
Served over TCP instead of the socket, nothing is let in without a
password or the token.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -unix-socket Ar path
Serve on this socket, for nginx; loopback clients are then let in
without a password.
.It Fl -port Ar port , Fl -bind Ar address
Serve on TCP instead; default port 8080 on every address.
.It Fl -no-tls
Plain HTTP, when something in front terminates TLS.
.It Fl -no-browser
Do not open a browser.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/kldload/webui-token
The bearer token, mode 0600, made on first run.
.It Pa /run/kldload/webui.sock
The socket.
.It Pa /usr/local/share/kldload-webui/
The pages.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
It serves until stopped.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Reading the token for a script; not run for this page:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# cat /etc/kldload/webui-token
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldload-proxy 8 ,
.Xr kldload-session 8 ,
.Xr kldload-tls-cert 8 ,
.Xr nginx 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-05-21 the WebSocket was found to accept any client that reached
the port, as root; the token was added.
On 2026-09-23 letting loopback in without a password was confined to the
unix socket.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Every process on the machine, whoever runs it, counts as local, and is
let in without a password.
On a machine with other users, or with services that could be broken
into, treat every account as able to act as root through the console.
Terminals it opens are reached at addresses that are themselves the only
credential; see
.Xr kldload-session 8 .
